From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] explorer: Task View, Alt+Tab and the desktop switch indicator at the display scale

Task View (0446 and on), the Alt+Tab switcher and the indicator shown on
switching desktops were drawn in fixed pixels: at 175% on a 2736x1824
screen (a Surface Pro 7, David 2026-10-05: "everything is tiny") their
text, tiles, icons and frames were 100%'s, small beside the 70 px taskbar.
They take the display scale (LogPixels, read as each opens, in eighths as
the taskbar does: 0832) for every size: the desktops' tiles, the windows'
grid and titles, the switcher's cells, the fonts. At 100% nothing changes.

Test: test/barhidpi-gate.sh with test/barhidpi-probe.c (the New desktop
tile 200 px at 100%, 350 px at 175%; mutant SG_MUTANT_TV_UNSCALED).
---
--- a/programs/explorer/vdesktop.c
+++ b/programs/explorer/vdesktop.c
@@ -77,6 +77,24 @@
 #define COL_ACCENT    RGB(0x8A,0x2B,0xE2)
 #define COL_HOVER     RGB(0x4A,0x4A,0x4A)
 
+/* Stained Glass OS: Task View, the Alt+Tab switcher and the desktop switch
+ * indicator at the display scale (LogPixels, as the taskbar: 0832), in
+ * eighths of 100%, read as each opens: on a 2736x1824 screen at 175% (a
+ * Surface Pro 7, David 2026-10-05) their text and tiles were 100%'s. */
+static int vd_s8 = 8;
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_TV_UNSCALED
+#define V(v) (((v) * vd_s8 + ((v) < 0 ? -4 : 4)) / 8)
+#else
+#define V(v) (v)
+#endif
+static void vd_load_scale(void)
+{
+    DWORD dpi = 96, size = sizeof(dpi);
+    RegGetValueW( HKEY_CURRENT_USER, L"Control Panel\\Desktop", L"LogPixels", RRF_RT_REG_DWORD, NULL, &dpi, &size );
+    if (dpi < 96) dpi = 96;
+    vd_s8 = (int)min( (dpi * 8 + 48) / 96, 32 );
+}
